  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New Jersey received $200M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 98.0% year over year. Award volume in FY2027 to date reached 943 awards, with an average award size of $212K. Historical context shows much larger annual totals: FY22 obligations were $9.5B, FY23 obligations were $9.4B, FY24 obligations were $10B, FY25 obligations were $9.6B, and FY26 obligations were $9.9B. Remediation Services is the largest industry in FY2027 to date at $40M. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency in FY2027 to date at $83.2M. CAPE-APTIM JV1, LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date at $40M. The FY2027 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date figures, and reflect early-year activity compared with full prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $200M, versus prior full-year totals that range from $9.4B to $10B. Obligations fell 98.0% year over year. Award count in FY2027 to date is 943 with an average award size of $212K, reflecting a much smaller, partial-year spending profile compared with full fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for the bulk of FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $83.2M and the Department of Defense obligated $41.4M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $33.1M and the Department of Transportation obligated $10.4M. CAPE-APTIM JV1, LLC received $40M and SK2 LLC received $31.8M in FY2027 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
